     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "On the beach Ravi felt cool air coming from the sea in the afternoon.\n\"That is a sea breeze,\" said his uncle."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "sea breeze",
     "absorb",
     "reflect"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "During the day land heats faster than water. Warm air over land rises and cool air from the sea moves in. This is the sea breeze. At night the land cools faster and the breeze reverses.\nWe wear dark clothes in winter because dark colours absorb heat, and light clothes in summer because light colours reflect heat.\nWoollen clothes keep us warm because they trap air, a poor conductor."
    }
   },
